Appendix D: Proof of Lemma 5.1 (Threshold Bound)

Lemma D.1 (Threshold bound, conditional). For every t \ge 0,

\sum_{j \in V} (d^{\mathrm{ALG}}_j - (2+O(\varepsilon))t)_+ \le (2+O(\varepsilon)) \sum_{j \in V} (d^*_j - t)_+.

Proof (with gaps). Consider the optimal solution and the guessed configuration that matches it. For each optimal cluster C, let p_C be its pivot (a sampled point from R or a facility from S). The guessing phase enumerates a radius parameter r_C for each cluster from a geometric progression; when the correct configuration is found, r_C \le (1+\varepsilon) \operatorname{radius}^*(C), where \operatorname{radius}^*(C) is the true radius of C.

The algorithm's construction ensures that for any client j \in C, the assigned facility \mu_{\mathrm{ALG}}(j) satisfies d(\mu_{\mathrm{ALG}}(j), p_C) \le \gamma t for some constant \gamma = O(\varepsilon). By the triangle inequality,

d^{\mathrm{ALG}}_j \le d(j, p_C) + d(p_C, \mu_{\mathrm{ALG}}(j)) \le d(j, p_C) + \gamma t.

Now fix a cluster C and consider two subsets:

· Close clients: C_{\le t} = \{j \in C : d^*_j \le t\}.
· Far clients: C_{>t} = \{j \in C : d^*_j > t\}.

Case 1: Close clients. For j \in C_{\le t},

d(j, p_C) \le d(j, \mu^*(j)) + d(\mu^*(j), p_C) \le d^*_j + r_C.

Since d^*_j \le t, we would like to bound r_C \le (1+\varepsilon)t. Gap A: r_C is the maximum distance over the entire cluster, including far clients with d^*_j > t. If any far client exists, r_C can be much larger than t, invalidating the bound. A corrected proof must partition the cluster into its close and far components and assign radii per component, or use a per-client radius derived from the guessing phase.

Conditional on Gap A being closed, we have d^{\mathrm{ALG}}_j \le t + (1+\varepsilon)t + \gamma t = (2+\varepsilon+\gamma)t. Choosing \gamma = O(\varepsilon) gives d^{\mathrm{ALG}}_j \le (2+O(\varepsilon))t, so close clients contribute zero to the left-hand side.

Case 2: Far clients. For j \in C_{>t},

d(j, p_C) \le d^*_j + r_C \le d^*_j + (1+\varepsilon) \operatorname{radius}^*(C) \le d^*_j + (1+\varepsilon) d^*_{\max},

where d^*_{\max} = \max_{j' \in C} d^*_{j'}. Since t \le d^*_j for far clients,

d^{\mathrm{ALG}}_j - (2+O(\varepsilon))t \le (2+O(\varepsilon))d^*_j - (2+O(\varepsilon))t + r_C = (2+O(\varepsilon))(d^*_j - t) + r_C.

Summing over j \in C_{>t},

\sum_{j \in C_{>t}} (d^{\mathrm{ALG}}_j - (2+O(\varepsilon))t)_+ \le (2+O(\varepsilon)) \sum_{j \in C_{>t}} (d^*_j - t) + |C_{>t}| r_C.

Gap B: We need to bound |C_{>t}| r_C in terms of \sum_{j \in C} (d^*_j - t)_+. The assertion

|C_{>t}| r_C \le (2+O(\varepsilon)) \sum_{j \in C} (d^*_j - t)_+

is not proved. A correct argument must show that the number of far clients times the cluster radius is controlled by the excess of the far clients over t. This is plausible when r_C \le (1+\varepsilon) \max_j d^*_j and t is at most a constant fraction of the maximum, but the constant must be tracked explicitly.

Conditional on Gap B being closed, summing over all clusters gives

\sum_{j \in V} (d^{\mathrm{ALG}}_j - (2+O(\varepsilon))t)_+ \le (2+O(\varepsilon)) \sum_{j \in V} (d^*_j - t)_+.

\square

Status. Lemma D.1 is conditional on closing Gap A and Gap B. The unweighted, unconstrained-outlier version is proved in Dai, Li & Peng (ICALP 2026, Lemma 5.2). Transferring it to the capacitated vector-search setting requires the two fixes above. This is Open Problem 2.

