Appendix E: Proof of Theorem 5.2 (Top-\ell Approximation)

Theorem E.1 (Top-\ell approximation, conditional on Lemma 5.1). For every \ell \in \{1, \dots, n\},

\|\mathbf{d}^{\mathrm{ALG}}\|_{\text{top-}\ell} \le (3+O(\varepsilon)) \|\mathbf{d}^*\|_{\text{top-}\ell}.

Proof. Let t^* = d^*_{(\ell)}, the \ell-th largest distance in the optimal solution. By Definition 2.4,

\|\mathbf{d}^*\|_{\text{top-}\ell} = \sum_{j \in V} (d^*_j - t^*)_+ + \ell t^*.

Set t = (1+\varepsilon)t^* to account for rounding. Apply Lemma D.1:

\sum_{j \in V} (d^{\mathrm{ALG}}_j - (2+O(\varepsilon))(1+\varepsilon)t^*)_+ \le (2+O(\varepsilon)) \sum_{j \in V} (d^*_j - (1+\varepsilon)t^*)_+.

Since (d^*_j - (1+\varepsilon)t^*)_+ \le (d^*_j - t^*)_+, the right-hand side is at most

(2+O(\varepsilon)) \sum_{j \in V} (d^*_j - t^*)_+.

Now use the variational form of the top-\ell norm with threshold (2+O(\varepsilon))(1+\varepsilon)t^*:

\|\mathbf{d}^{\mathrm{ALG}}\|_{\text{top-}\ell} \le \sum_{j \in V} (d^{\mathrm{ALG}}_j - (2+O(\varepsilon))(1+\varepsilon)t^*)_+ + \ell (2+O(\varepsilon))(1+\varepsilon)t^*.

Substituting the bound from Lemma D.1,

\|\mathbf{d}^{\mathrm{ALG}}\|_{\text{top-}\ell} \le (2+O(\varepsilon)) \sum_{j \in V} (d^*_j - t^*)_+ + (2+O(\varepsilon))(1+\varepsilon) \ell t^*.

Since (1+\varepsilon) = 1+O(\varepsilon),

\|\mathbf{d}^{\mathrm{ALG}}\|_{\text{top-}\ell} \le (2+O(\varepsilon)) \left( \sum_{j \in V} (d^*_j - t^*)_+ + \ell t^* \right) + O(\varepsilon) \ell t^*.

Because \ell t^* \le \|\mathbf{d}^*\|_{\text{top-}\ell},

\|\mathbf{d}^{\mathrm{ALG}}\|_{\text{top-}\ell} \le (2+O(\varepsilon)) \|\mathbf{d}^*\|_{\text{top-}\ell} + O(\varepsilon) \|\mathbf{d}^*\|_{\text{top-}\ell} = (3+O(\varepsilon)) \|\mathbf{d}^*\|_{\text{top-}\ell}.

\square

Remark. The proof is conditional on Lemma D.1. The same argument appears in Dai, Li & Peng (ICALP 2026, Theorem 3.2) for the unweighted, unconstrained-outlier case.

